{"title":"Crescent Dental Labs","sub":"Can a fund triple its money on dental labs?","type":"Private equity","industry":"Healthcare services","geo":"United States","diff":2,"fmt":"Interviewer-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Private equity returns · buy-and-build · value-creation bridge","prompt":"A private equity fund is looking at Crescent, which makes crowns and dentures for dentists across the Midwest. Crescent has $10M of EBITDA and the owners want 8×: $80M. The fund needs at least 2.5× its money in five years. The deal partner's plan is to buy small local labs and fold them into Crescent. Does the deal work?","clarify":[{"q":"Financing?","a":"Half debt, half fund equity: $40M each."},{"q":"Organic growth?","a":"About 4% a year from more procedures and an ageing population."},{"q":"Add-ons?","a":"There are hundreds of small labs. The fund expects to buy 10 over five years, each with about $1M of EBITDA, at about 5×, funded with extra debt."},{"q":"Cash and exit?","a":"Crescent's cash flow can repay about $20M of debt over five years. Lab groups of Crescent's size or larger sell for about 9× EBITDA."}],"structure":{"root":"Will the fund make 2.5× in five years?","branches":[{"head":"Entry","items":["Price, debt and equity"]},{"head":"Value creation","items":["Organic growth","Add-on acquisitions","Debt repayment"]},{"head":"Exit","items":["EBITDA × exit multiple − debt"]},{"head":"Risks","items":["Integrating labs","Exit multiple","Dentists' consolidation"]}]},"hypothesis":"Organic growth of 4% alone won't get to 2.5×. The returns probably depend on buying small labs cheaply and selling them as part of a bigger group at a higher multiple.","questions":[{"q":"First, what return would Crescent deliver without any add-ons?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>EBITDA in year 5: $10M × 1.04⁵ = $12.2M. Exit value at 9×: $109M. Debt: $40M − $20M = $20M. Equity: <b>$89M</b>.</p> <p>Return: $89M ÷ $40M = <b>2.24×</b> (about 17% a year), below the 2.5× target.</p>"},{"q":"Now add the buy-and-build plan.","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"383.56pt\" height=\"205.56pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 383.56 205.56\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M -0 205.56 L 383.56 205.56 L 383.56 0 L -0 0 L -0 205.56 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 30.4 160.16 L 376.36 160.16 L 376.36 10.472 L 30.4 10.472 L 30.4 160.16 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"><g id=\"xtick_1\"><g id=\"line2d_1\"><defs><path id=\"ma99844d2ee\" d=\"M 0 0 L 0 3.5 \" style=\"stroke: #4a5568; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></defs><g><use xlink:href=\"#ma99844d2ee\" x=\"62.974156\" y=\"160.16\" style=\"fill: #4a5568; stroke: #4a5568; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_1\"><g style=\"fill: #4a5568\" transform=\"translate(47.474781 175.36) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-22\" d=\"M 3322 0 L 595 0 L 595 4467 L 3322 4467 L 3322 3994 L 1133 3994 L 1133 2496 L 3194 2496 L 3194 2022 L 1133 2022 L 1133 474 L 3322 474 L 3322 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-14\" d=\"M 2656 -1280 L 2656 538 L 2630 538 Q 2483 230 2243 76 Q 2003 -77 1664 -77 Q 1254 -77 950 134 Q 646 346 483 736 Q 320 1126 320 1651 Q 320 2182 483 2569 Q 646 2957 950 3168 Q 1254 3379 1664 3379 Q 2003 3379 2252 3228 Q 2502 3078 2630 2765 L 2656 2765 L 2656 3302 L 3168 3302 L 3168 -1280 L 2656 -1280 z\nM 1805 384 Q 2042 384 2234 464 Q 2426 544 2541 694 Q 2656 845 2656 1056 L 2656 2285 Q 2656 2470 2541 2611 Q 2426 2752 2234 2835 Q 2042 2918 1805 2918 Q 1376 2918 1123 2646 Q 870 2374 870 1933 L 870 1370 Q 870 928 1123 656 Q 1376 384 1805 384 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-18\" d=\"M 2579 0 L 2579 538 L 2554 538 Q 2458 301 2250 112 Q 2042 -77 1626 -77 Q 1120 -77 816 252 Q 5